pmdomain: give imx8m_blk_ctrl_domain_data the errata flag the chain's power-on
path already tests.

Adapted from
  https://cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v6.x/incr/patch-6.12.96-97.xz

6.12.96-97 taught imx8m_blk_ctrl_power_on() to gate VC8000E's clocks around the
reset (errata err050531) behind a per-domain flag; those hunks applied, the
struct member did not, so the file does not compile. Only the member is added
here, defaulting to false: no domain in this vendor tree sets it (the upstream
table hunk targets a domain layout this tree does not have), so the workaround
stays off exactly as published.

--- a/drivers/pmdomain/imx/imx8m-blk-ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/imx/imx8m-blk-ctrl.c
@@ -77,6 +77,15 @@
 	notifier_fn_t power_notifier_fn;
 	const struct imx8m_blk_ctrl_hurry_data *hurry_data;
 	const struct imx8m_blk_ctrl_noc_data *noc_data[DOMAIN_MAX_NOC];
+
+	/*
+	 * VC8000E reset de-assertion edge and AXI clock may have a timing issue.
+	 * Workaround: Set bit2 (vc8000e_clk_en) of BLK_CLK_EN_CSR to 0 to gate off
+	 * both AXI clock and VC8000E clock sent to VC8000E and AXI clock sent to
+	 * VPU_NOC m_v_2 interface during VC8000E power up(VC8000E reset is
+	 * de-asserted by HW)
+	 */
+	bool is_errata_err050531;
 };
 
 #define DOMAIN_MAX_CLKS 4
